Description: treat an uncomputed mergeability as a wait instead of a query error
Author: Azhou AI Hub
Forwarded: no

GitHub computes mergeable and mergeStateStatus on the first read that asks, and
`gh pr view` reports a field it has not filled in as "" the same way it reports a
missing review decision. parsePullRequest raised that as a missing-key query
error, so the watcher backed off with exponential delay and exited 7 instead of
looking again at the ordinary poll interval. An uncomputed mergeability is now
read as UNKNOWN and holds the watcher on the polling interval until GitHub has
an answer.

